			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823606">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My overall feeling regarding this is: so what?</p>
<p>There's weird little implications scattered throughout: from the handprints fitting Tradias' hand to the holes appearing to the change of the things movement corresponding to a flight; but none of these feel like they piece together into a coherent whole? Like, it's dangerous and it's heading towards someone but&#8230;why?</p>
<p>There's little structural things like the actuality of what a Centimane event is being the last thing described; when really saying what it is and then when it will happen would be more effective; and a general feeling of your ConProcs/Description paragraphs being unassociated sentences over a coherent paragraph; but fundamentally, my issue is that at the end, this doesn't give me enough pieces to collapse it into a whole that feels satisfying.</p>
<p>It kinda feels like this has a lot of opportunity for some really evocative description of the hands and stuff, particularly within the video log, but instead it feels like it spends a lot of time having Tradia mumble about being lost or what the air is like, and it feels like it just&#8230;needs more content there? Like you could theoretically cut basically everything Tradia says out the log and it'd still convey much the same thing; and indeed it's only really the final four action notes that actually convey things, and I'm left&#8230;wanting? Even if it's just more of an emotional arc from Tradia where we can see him go from calm and collected and scientific at the start to running scared and frightened at the end (which, he does but it's conveyed entirely through his behaviour with only a few hints in the dialogue).</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>Gonna note that I can miss stuff; flag things which are right as being wrong and indeed flag things which are deliberately wrong.</em><br />
<em>I'll likely use <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">strikethrough</span> to indicate stuff to remove and <span style="color: green">green text</span> to indicate stuff to add.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Guards are to <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">be patrolling</span><span style="color: green">patrol</span> the area around SCP-X in routines 1 hour apart.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'in routines 1 hour apart' feels unclear: if you mean e.g. 'with 1 hour between patrols', perhaps that would be a clearer phrasing?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the case of a Centimane event, nearby human population centers will be evacuated under the pretense of an unavoidable future dust storm.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd probably add a paragraph break here cos of the change in topic from guard patrols to Centimane events; and I'd lean towards moving the part of the description describing them to a footnote here</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After the evacuation of the population center, SCP-X will be closely monitored for the point where it exits the area. Afterward, Foundation funds will go into repairing the damage done to buildings and other structures by SCP-X.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This kinda implies these two things are related but they aren't quite; it feels like the 'point where it exits the area' needs a little more clarification around why it's important for this to work.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-X is a geoglyph located in an uninhabited desert area in ██████.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels like a weird redaction; it kinda feels like this would be more effective if we knew where it was so we can imagine what places are in danger.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The lines making up SCP-X are, on average, 1.5cm deep, 3cm thick, and stylized in the shape of a human hand, covering roughly 24km<sup>2</sup>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This phrasing is ambiguous as to whether each individual line looks like a human hand or the overall geoglyph looks like a human hand.</p>
<p>If you want the second, I'd add replace the comma between '1.5cm deep' and '3cm thick' with an and, and change the comma after 'thick' to a semi-colon. If you want the first, I'd separate the region they're covering into a separate sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>being capable of traveling 17m in a day.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like this could do with a more evocative word than 'travelling'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Most electronic devices that are put inside of SCP-X malfunction, leading to difficulty in finding possible internal anomalous phenomena within SCP-X.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'Most' is needlessly vague here imo. I'd either cut it, or give an indication of what causes some electronic devices to break. Same goes for 'malfunction' tbh.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Most electronic devices that are put inside of SCP-X malfunction, leading to difficulty in finding possible internal anomalous phenomena within SCP-X. Any attempts at installing barriers to prevent the movement of SCP-X have been met with failure. The soonest possible date of a Centimane event is 3 years and 163 days. See Addendum X-01.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These three sentences don't feel like they belong in the same paragraph: they're all completely disconnected ideas with no flow from one to the next to the last.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 07/10/20██<span style="color: green">,</span> Agent Johnathan Tradia was tasked with an exploration mission into SCP-X to ascertain any other possible anomalous properties.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not a fan of this redaction; I'm not sure why when this occurred would be sensitive information.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Tradia. ]</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>this space is unnecessary; here and every where you use it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>[Tradia proceeds walking for two minutes and thirty-seven seconds. ]</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Walking where?</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Agent Tradia:</strong> Huh, the ground in here seems pretty weird. It's stretchy, it's kinda like a trampoline.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why does it take Tradia like, 2.5minutes to notice this?</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Tradia resumes walking for approximately three minutes before turning around, showing multiple hand-shaped indentations on the ground. The handprints form a line leading to Tradia. ]</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing an opening [ here</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 08/12/██ SCP-4440 ceased movement, rotated 37° clockwise, and resumed movement resulting in a delay of 73 days until a Centimane event will occur.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>1) this is a bad redaction again</p>
<p>2) This addendum as a whole doesn't really feel like it builds off what came before.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
</div>
</div>

